Description:

On TLS 1.3 connections, the channel binding for SCRAM-*-PLUS and other
channel-binding SASL mechanisms is now ``tls-exporter`` (RFC 9266) instead of
``tls-unique``, which TLS 1.3 doesn't define.  TLS 1.2 connections still use
``tls-unique``.


Documentation:

None.


Config changes:

None.


Upgrade instructions:

Clients that send ``tls-unique`` channel binding over TLS 1.3 will fail to
authenticate with -PLUS mechanisms, and must switch to ``tls-exporter`` as
RFC 9266 requires.  Such clients were getting no channel binding protection
on TLS 1.3 before.  Clients that don't use channel binding are unaffected.


